    "problem_statement": "omdict1D.add() returns None instead of self after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `add()` method in `omdict1D` class is now returning `None` instead of returning `self`, breaking method chaining functionality.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom furl.omdict1D import omdict1D\n\nomd = omdict1D()\nresult = omd.add('key', 'value')\nprint(result)  # Expected: <omdict1D object>, Actual: None\n\n# Method chaining also broken\nomd = omdict1D()\ntry:\n    omd.add('a', '1').add('b', '2')  # This will fail\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")  # 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'add'\n```\n\nThe `add()` method should return `self` to allow for method chaining, but it's currently returning `None`."
